# Packages of the amd64-efi target, on top of profiles/base/packages: Debian's
# amd64 kernel and GRUB's environment tool (RAUC's grub backend).
linux-image-amd64
grub-common
# Intel firmware that Debian 13 split out of firmware-misc-nonfree
# (profiles/base/packages.debian): the i915 graphics firmware (DMC for the
# display's power states, GuC, HuC for media) and the Sound Open Firmware of
# Intel Smart Sound audio, both on most x86 IPCs and panel PCs since about
# 2019.
firmware-intel-graphics
firmware-sof-signed
# The Secure Boot chain (ADR-0011), which build/mkimage.sh copies onto the
# IRONFLOCKOS partition: Debian's shim, signed by Microsoft; MokManager, which
# shim starts when a check fails; Debian's signed GRUB. Debian's kernels are
# signed already. Listed here so packages.tsv and the SBOM carry them.
shim-signed
shim-helpers-amd64-signed
grub-efi-amd64-signed
# fwupd's UEFI capsule helper, signed by Debian: capsule updates (lane 3)
# also start with Secure Boot on.
fwupd-amd64-signed
# The splash (docs/build.md, "The screen"): Plymouth with its script plugin,
# which draws IronFlockOS's theme; the label plugin and fontconfig with
# DejaVu, for the message line below the picture; all of it also in the
# initramfs, with the kernel's graphics drivers (Plymouth's initramfs hook).
plymouth
plymouth-label
fontconfig
